## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to craft branchless 128-bit comparison, a common low-level operation in high-performance contexts.

## Key Concepts

- Branchless selection using masks
- 128-bit comparison via hi/lo parts
- Handling -1/0/1 outputs reliably

## Code Example

```c
int compare128(uint128 a, uint128 b) {
  int hi = (int)(a.hi > b.hi) - (int)(a.hi < b.hi);
  int lo = (int)(a.lo > b.lo) - (int)(a.lo < b.lo);
  int t  = (hi != 0);
  int m  = -t;
  return (hi & m) | (lo & ~m);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adapt to unsigned 128-bit values?
- How would you extend to return an enum instead of int?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to apply bit-hacking techniques across a 128-bit value by splitting into two 64-bit halves and summing, without loops or branches.

## Key Concepts

- 64-bit popcount via parallel bit counting masks
- Treat 128-bit as two 64-bit blocks
- No loops or branches; purely bitwise ops

## Code Example

```c
typedef struct { uint64_t hi; uint64_t lo; } uint128;
static inline uint64_t popcount64(uint64_t x){
  x = x - ((x >> 1) & 0x5555555555555555ULL);
  x = (x & 0x3333333333333333ULL) + ((x >> 2) & 0x3333333333333333ULL);
  x = (x + (x >> 4)) & 0x0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0fULL;
  x = x + (x >> 8);
  x = x + (x >> 16);
  x = x + (x >> 32);
  return x & 0x7f;
}
unsigned int countBits128(uint128 x){
  return popcount64(x.hi) + popcount64(x.lo);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you leverage __builtin_popcountll if available?
- How would you generalize to 256-bit types?

## Why This Is Asked
Targeted to assess bit‑manipulation proficiency across multi‑word integers, with emphasis on branchless design and fixed work per input.

## Key Concepts
- XOR for difference on multi-word values
- 64-bit popcount with masks and shifts
- Branchless accumulation across halves

## Code Example
```javascript
// Sketch (C-like)
int hammingDistance128(uint128 a, uint128 b){
  uint64_t lo = (a.lo ^ b.lo);
  uint64_t hi = (a.hi ^ b.hi);
  lo = lo - ((lo >> 1) & 0x5555555555555555ULL);
  lo = (lo & 0x3333333333333333ULL) + ((lo >> 2) & 0x3333333333333333ULL);
  lo = (lo + (lo >> 4)) & 0x0F0F0F0F0F0F0F0FULL;
  uint64_t countLo = (lo * 0x0101010101010101ULL) >> 56;
  hi = hi - ((hi >> 1) & 0x5555555555555555ULL);
  hi = (hi & 0x3333333333333333ULL) + ((hi >> 2) & 0x3333333333333333ULL);
  hi = (hi + (hi >> 4)) & 0x0F0F0F0F0F0F0F0FULL;
  uint64_t countHi = (hi * 0x0101010101010101ULL) >> 56;
  return (int)(countLo + countHi);
}
```

